WHAT WAS TAKEN AND WHAT WAS CHANGED. Thirteen glyphs are used by
`src/data/transitVehicleIcons.js` to draw live French transit vehicles by
class: airport_shuttle, cable_car, directions_boat, directions_bus,
directions_railway, flight, funicular, local_taxi, monorail, subway, train,
tram, trolley.

Only the single `d` path string of each glyph is vendored, verbatim and
unmodified, into that module — the surrounding SVG document is not. At render
time each path is drawn TWICE by this project: once as a wide dark stroke (a
halo, so the glyph stays readable over pale terrain) and once as a white fill
(so Cesium's per-billboard colour multiply can tint it by vehicle class). The
path geometry itself is untouched.
